# Sidebar tab system (Clutter editor)

## Workspace tabs

Rail tabs (see `SidebarTabs.tsx`): **Notes** | **Calendar** | **Tasks** | **Tags**.

| Tab ID (code) | Label | Tab component | Status |
|---------------|-------|---------------|--------|
| `notes` | Notes | `NotesTab` | In progress — spec below |
| `journals` | Calendar | TBD | Not specified yet |
| `tasks` | Tasks | `TasksTab` | Spec below |
| `tags` | Tags | `TagsTab` | Shell below — tag rows TBD |

Each tab that uses the sidebar list pattern: `{Name}Tab.tsx` + `SidebarPanel`. Other tabs will be documented when specified.

---

## Notes tab — information architecture

### Navigation (pinned, not scrolled)

`SidebarPanel` → `navigation`:

| Row | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| Section header | **Notes** (static label) |
| All notes | Top-level nav destination |
| Templates | Top-level nav destination |
| Inbox | Top-level nav destination |

### Scrollable content

`SidebarPanel` → direct `<Section>` children (no wrapper div):

| Section | Contents |
|---------|----------|
| **Favorites** | Mix of **notes** and **folders** (user-curated shortcuts) |
| **Folders** | **Folders only** — root of the folder tree |

Both sections are collapsible; header click navigates, chevron toggles expand (see Section props).

---

## Notes tree — folders vs notes

Recursive tree under Favorites and Folders. Map from data in the tab; `InteractiveItem` only renders affordances.

### Folder row

- `hasInlineCaret` — leading column + caret (do not pass `hasInlineSlot`).
- `hasChildren` — from data (`childIds.length > 0` or equivalent).
  - **Has children:** caret is clickable; `onExpandToggle` + `isExpanded`; reveals nested notes and subfolders.
  - **Empty folder:** caret visible but **disabled** (dimmed slot, `pointer-events: none`); row still `onClick`-able to open the folder.
- A folder may contain **notes** and **subfolders**; subfolders repeat the same rules recursively.

### Note row (leaf)

- `hasInlineSlot` **only** — alignment column, **no caret icon**.
- Always `onClick` + `active` from `destination`; never `onExpandToggle`.

### Why notes use an empty slot

Folders use the caret column; notes use an empty slot of the same width so icons and labels line up across row types.

### Tree indent (nested rows)

Indent is defined on **`InteractiveItem`** (`variant="default"` only), not per-tab CSS.

| Piece | Value |
|-------|--------|
| CSS token | `--interactive-item-indent-step` = `var(--space-16)` → **16px** per level |
| Prop | `indentDepth?: number` (default `0`) |
| Row padding | `padding-left: 6px + indentDepth × 16px` (base 6px is row padding, not repeated per level) |

**Not automatic:** the tree renderer must pass `indentDepth` for each row. `InteractiveItem` does not infer depth from `hasInlineCaret` / parent expand state.

**Who passes depth:** recursive row helpers in each tab — e.g. `NotesTreeRow`, `TaskSidebarRow` — with `depth = 0` at group top-level and `depth + 1` for each child rendered under an expanded `hasInlineCaret` parent.

Applies to:

- Notes: nested notes/folders under an expanded folder
- Tasks: subtasks under an expanded task
- Any future sidebar tree using the same pattern

Nav rows, section headers, subheaders, and placeholders do **not** use `indentDepth`.

